 systems to support their functions within several contexts—including criminal justice, education, and benefits provision—with important consequences for accountability, privacy, social inequity, and public participation in decision-making. We explore the social implications of municipal algorithmic systems across a variety of stages, including problem formulation, technology acquisition, deployment, and evaluation. We highlight several open questions that require further empirical research."}]", "excerpt_truncated": true, "source_sha256": "846fbdd52b824b1146f568e0d8edc888cf3e0dd281e7d868175b86c2dd0bc61b", "verification_required": true, "topic_domain": "assumption_challenge", "evidence_role": "discovery", "host_tier": "discovery", "source_identity": null, "persistent_identifiers": ["doi:10.1145/3178876.3186138", "doi:10.1146/annurev-lawsocsci-041221-023808", "openalex:W2964316623", "openalex:W3172101419"], "source_candidates": ["https://doi.org/10.1145/3178876.3186138", "https://doi.org/10.1146/annurev-lawsocsci-041221-023808"], "source_candidate_identities": {}}
